  <h1>Lesson 18: Buttons & Links Styling in CSS</h1>
  <p>Learn Hover Effects, Cursor Pointer, Transition, Beautiful Buttons & Links | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. Why Buttons Matter?</h2>
    <p>A button is the <b>most clicked thing</b> on a website - Buy Now, Sign Up, Contact Us, Download.</p>
    <p>If your button looks plain, nobody will click it. If it looks beautiful with hover effect, people will click it.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> Facebook Login button (blue), YouTube Subscribe button (red), Daraz Buy Now button (orange) - all are styled buttons.</div>
    <h2>2. Normal Button vs Styled Button</h2>
    <div class="result"><b>Normal Button (No CSS - Ugly):</b><br><button style="margin-top:8px">Submit</button><br><br><b>Styled Button (With CSS - Beautiful):</b><br><button class="demo-btn" style="margin-top:8px">Submit →</button></div>
    <h2>3. Basic Button CSS - Copy This</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.btn</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">padding</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">12px 25px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Top-Bottom 12px, Left-Right 25px */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">border</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">none</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">border-radius</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">8px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">font-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">16px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">font-weight</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">bold</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">cursor</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">pointer</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Hand icon on hover */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><button class="demo-btn">Click Me</button><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Move your mouse over the button - cursor becomes a hand 👆 because of <b>cursor: pointer;</b></p></div>
    <h2>4. :hover - Magic Effect</h2>
    <p><b>:hover</b> means "When mouse goes over this element, change its style."</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.btn</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">transition</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">0.3s</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Smooth change - Very Important! */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn:hover</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#1d4ed8</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Darker blue on hover */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">transform</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">scale(1.05)</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Slightly bigger */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Try Hovering:</b><br><br><button class="demo-btn">Hover Me - I Grow!</button><p style="margin:8px 0 0"><b>Without transition:</b> Color changes suddenly - looks bad.<br><b>With transition: 0.3s;</b> Color changes smoothly - looks professional.</p></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Golden Rule:</b> Always add <b>transition: 0.3s;</b> to every button and link. It makes hover smooth.</div>
    <h2>5. 4 Button Styles - Copy These for Projects</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 1. Normal Button */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 2. Outline Button - Only border, no fill */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn-outline</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">border</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">2px solid #2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn-outline:hover</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 3. Gradient Button */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn-gradient</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">linear-gradient(90deg, #2563eb, #16a34a)</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 4. Round Button - Pill Shape */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.btn-round</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">border-radius</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">50px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - 4 Styles - Hover Each One:</b><br><br><button class="demo-btn">1. Normal Button</button><button class="demo-btn-outline" style="margin-left:8px">2. Outline Button</button><br><br><button class="demo-btn-gradient">3. Gradient Button</button><button class="demo-btn" style="border-radius:50px;margin-left:8px">4. Round Button</button></div>
    <h2>6. Links Styling - 4 States</h2>
    <p>A link has 4 states. Learn them in order - <b>L</b>o<b>V</b>e <b>HA</b>te trick: <b>Link → Visited → Hover → Active</b></p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>State</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td>:link</td><td>Normal link - Not clicked yet</td><td>a:link { color: blue; }</td></tr>
      <tr><td>:visited</td><td>Link already clicked before</td><td>a:visited { color: purple; }</td></tr>
      <tr><td>:hover</td><td>Mouse is over link</td><td>a:hover { color: red; }</td></tr>
      <tr><td>:active</td><td>Link is being clicked now</td><td>a:active { color: green; }</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">a</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#2563eb</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">text-decoration</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">none</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Remove underline */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">font-weight</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">bold</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">transition</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">0.3s</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">a:hover</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#dc2626</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">text-decoration</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">underline</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Hover This Link:</b><br><a href="#" class="demo-link">👉 Click Here - I Change Color on Hover</a></div>
    <h2>7. Link as Button - Very Useful</h2>
    <p>Sometimes you want a link that looks like a button. Just add <b>class="btn"</b> to an &lt;a&gt; tag.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"/contact"</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"btn"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Contact Us</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><br><a href="#" class="demo-btn" style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;margin-top:8px">Contact Us →</a><p style="margin:8px 0 0">This looks like a button, but it is actually a link. It goes to another page when clicked.</p></div>
    <h2>8. Full Example - Call to Action Section</h2>
    <div class="result"><div style="background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:30px 20px;border-radius:12px;text-align:center"><h2 style="color:white;margin:0">Start Learning Today</h2><p style="color:#cbd5e1;margin:10px 0">Free HTML CSS JS Course - No fees, No signup.</p><button class="demo-btn-green">Start Learning Free →</button><button class="demo-btn-outline" style="margin-left:8px">View All Lessons</button></div></div>
    <h2>9. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>In Playground, make this:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>Normal Button</b> - blue, white text, padding 12px 25px, border-radius 8px, cursor pointer<br>2. One <b>Outline Button</b> - white background, blue border, on hover blue background + white text<br>3. One <b>Link</b> - no underline, on hover red color + underline<br>4. Add <b>transition: 0.3s;</b> to all</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Button = background + color + padding + border-radius + cursor: pointer | :hover = Style when mouse goes over | transition: 0.3s; = Smooth change | cursor: pointer; = Hand icon | Link States = :link, :visited, :hover, :active (LoVe HAte) | Outline Button = border only, no fill | Link as Button = &lt;a class="btn"&gt;</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson19">Lesson 19 - Forms Styling</a> to learn how to style inputs, labels and forms beautifully.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
